From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:57:37 -0400
Subject: fix: the checks round of 2026-10-18

The BACKLOG's checks still owed, each turned into tests that go through the
user's path where a test can ask the question, with the faults they found:

- The core loop (S-173): the drags onto a folder header and onto a Space
  chip, in the open sidebar and in the rail, through the window (TST-7); a
  row selected before its folder collapsed leaves the selection, and Copy
  Link on a split alone copies the one pane (TST-8); the core chords reach
  their commands as keys, and a window that stops being active ends the
  Control-Tab run (TST-9).
- Spaces and their jars (S-147): a session cookie in a Space's jar comes
  back after a restart; a Space pin taken to another window keeps its pin
  and home; a deleted Space's jar is wiped at once and its directory goes
  at the next start, through Chromium's storage-partition collection, which
  now keeps only the jars a Space names; replaced contents come back from
  the crash bubble's Restore.
- Every deletion of a Space asks first, from the title row's menu, a chip
  and Settings' bin, naming the Space, its tabs and where they go; each bin
  is named for its Space; another window's new or deleted Space reaches the
  title row (S-148).
- Rename Space edits in the title row, and in a small dialog on the rail or
  wherever the row is too narrow to type in; a rename left open when the
  sidebar collapses ends there, keeping what was typed, and every rename
  shows an unnamed Space's name greyed (S-149).
- A Space's last tab leaving for another window wakes no other Space's tab
  (S-150).
- Restored tabs and the product path (S-174): Escape in the command bar
  leaves the focus on the page; a Blank Window's isolation rows work; a tab
  just left is not archived at once, and the archive's idle time is
  wall-clock time kept in the session, so a night asleep and the time the
  browser was closed count (TST-18); a second Arc import adds no history
  visit twice and files a tab Arc added to a known folder; the bookmark bar
  goes with the conversion; a loading tab no longer keeps the last tab's
  row colour; the width slider keeps a dragged width; a Markdown link
  escapes its brackets; an unnamed Space exports under its shown name.
- Rows seen only live (S-128): a folder's rows keep their spacing in the
  rail; a white page's focused field and dropdown are white; the end of a
  reload keeps the page's row colour; the product name in every language.
- Partial rows (S-129, S-141): the sidebar's downloads button is bound to
  the action and hands a download over at once; a shared tab group draws
  no other Space's row; T11's first choice reads its label; the rail's
  favicons follow the density; the hover-expanded rail draws the
  essentials grid; the strip's height is shared after the title row is
  counted, so a short window cuts no row off.
- Full screen on the Mac (S-154): a tab switch re-themes the row, and a
  hovered rail no longer moves the back button. macOS 26's title-bar scroll
  pocket no longer draws its separator under the row (S-223), and with the
  row sliding in on demand the sidebar keeps the window's top row, so the
  Clear line is never under the traffic lights (S-224).
- Deleting a Space that another window was showing no longer stops the
  browser: that window names the Space it shows next before moving the tabs
  (S-222).
- A split whose contents were replaced keeps its split and group in the
  session (S-225).
- A read of the page's top edge before the page painted comes back
  transparent, which is no colour: the row had shown it as black at every
  reload on Windows, and for good in a private window on the ASan build
  (S-226).
- A pin the model files from what a tab carried (a drop from another
  window, a restore) is announced, so its row is drawn over the Clear line;
  on Windows the row of a pin dropped back stayed under it (pins H1, H2).
- The command bar lists the active Space's tabs first (K2); Cmd-W on a pin
  shows a row of its Space, never an essential (H3); Settings' shortcut
  notes no longer speak of rounds.
- A tab closed while its page's beforeunload answer changed (it turns
  after 500 ms) was never told it was being detached for deletion, so a
  sidebar row kept a pointer to it after it was freed: upstream's
  CloseWebContentses asked twice and told the tab only on matching
  answers. Each closed tab is now told exactly once (S-250).
- The toolbar's download button could stay hidden when horizontal tabs
  hand downloads back to it: the row is 26 DIP tall and the pinned
  buttons 28, so a container measured mid-slide never fitted, hid, and
  had no size to grow back from. The pinned-actions and extensions
  containers are measured by the row's width alone (S-250).
- A Space model going before its window's tab strip left its detach
  callback, which holds it unretained, on the strip.

Why: each item is behaviour its spec states, a defect a user meets, or a
crash.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next rebase folds each fix into the patch
that owns its code (patches/README.md, the round-patch exception).
